I dislike this usage, because "turning" originally meant the idea of
forcing undead to flee or be destroyed.  Unfortunately, the (presumably
later-added) corpse revivification bit is now the primary usage of the
spell/wand, which has both corrupted the meaning of the term and led to
a helluva lotta confusion.

If anything, I'd add something to the effect of "'Turning undead' has
multiple meanings: 1) The ability to force undead to flee or be
destroyed; and 2) The side effect of reviving corpses.  The #turn
extended command, when used by a class with the intrinsic #turn
ability, will only accomplish the former.  The latter is a side effect
as a result of the spell or wand."

Blame the devteam for *further* confusing matters by making #turn cast
the spell if you've learnt it as a non-holy-warrior type, I suppose.
(And why not?  Seems like a lot of blame has been hitting the devteam
on this newsgroup lately ;-) ).

